---
// Sieves (#/sieves[/<sailing>]): how training itself is measured, layer by layer. In the voyage
// vocabulary: the wind is the error on each guess, a tack is one update, trim is how it is set. The
// sieves read each layer's tacks: push (how hard the wind pushes it), move (how far its sail moves)
// and heading (which way it steers). The write-ups are fleet.SIEVES's own, never rewritten here.
---
<div class="section" id="sievesguide">
  <h1>Sieves <span class="q">how the ship answers the wind, layer by layer: how hard each layer is pushed, how far it moves, and which way it steers</span></h1>
  <section class="panel">
    <p class="lede">The <b>wind</b> is the error on each guess: how far the bet was from the word that came, felt by every weight that took part. A <b>tack</b> is the ship's answer, one training update: its direction from the wind, its size from the learning rate. <b>Trim</b> is how the tack is set. The three sieves read every layer's tacks, every 50 steps; a <b>kink</b> (◆) is the step where a layer changes regime, the break of a two-line fit, firm after <span id="kinkrule"></span>.</p>
  </section>
  <div class="cards" id="sievecards"></div>
  <section class="panel">
    <h2>One sailing, sieve by sieve <span class="note">rows are the layers, the bottom of the stack at the bottom; ◆ marks each layer's kink in its push</span></h2>
    <div class="handtools"><select id="sievepick" title="the sailing shown"></select><span class="note" id="sievenote"></span></div>
  </section>
  <section class="panel"><h2>Push <span class="note">log10 of the pre-clip gradient norm reaching each layer</span></h2><div class="chart" id="sieve-push"></div></section>
  <section class="panel"><h2>Move <span class="note">log10 of the change in each layer's weights over 50 steps, as a share of their size</span></h2><div class="chart" id="sieve-move"></div></section>
  <section class="panel"><h2>Heading <span class="note">the cosine between each layer's last two moves: 1 holds its angle, 0 wanders, below 0 comes about</span></h2><div class="chart" id="sieve-heading"></div></section>
  <section class="panel">
    <h2>Settled <span class="note">for each layer, the first step its heading stays at 0.8 or more for three records running, beside the step any star lit in that layer; do headings settle from the bottom up, and does a layer settle when its star lights?</span></h2>
    <div class="scroll"><table id="settledtable"><thead><tr><th>layer</th><th>heading settled at</th><th>heading now</th><th>push kink</th><th>stars lit in this layer</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div>
  </section>
</div>
